# Jace, Telepath Unbound's -3: "You may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard this turn. If that spell
# would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead." Memory Lapse's "if that spell is countered this way, put it on top of
# its owner's library instead of into that player's graveyard" replaces the same move to the graveyard (CR 614.1a), so the
# spell's controller chooses which applies (CR 616.1). Turn 1 Bot1 sacrifices Black Lotus for three Lightning Bolts; Jace
# loots on turn 5, flips with five cards in the graveyard, and his -3 lets a Bolt be cast from there at Bot2. Bot2 counters it
# with Memory Lapse, and Bot1 takes Jace's exile first: the Bolt is exiled, not put on top of Bot1's library, and Memory
# Lapse's no longer applies (CR 616.1f). Bot2 took the first three Bolts only: 20 - 9.

